  - id: the_wrath_revealed
    displayName: The Wrath Revealed
    flavorText: God's wrath is revealed against all ungodliness as Gentile and Jew
      alike stand exposed as guilty before God, with every mouth stopped and none
      found righteous.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Establishes that both Gentiles (who suppress the truth about God evident
      in creation and conscience) and Jews (who possess the law but do not keep it)
      stand equally guilty before God, so that every mouth is stopped and the whole
      world held accountable - the necessary foundation before a righteousness apart
      from the law can be introduced.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_romans
    managerId: the_wrath_revealed
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 70.96668207625552
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
    baseInkPerSecond: 3.5483341038127763
    unlockAtVerseIndex: 17
    managerName: 
    managerFlavorText: 
    managerUnlockLevel: 0
    managerUnlockAtVerseIndex: 0
    managerBonusMultiplier: 0.25
    managerUnlockCost: 0
    submanagers: []
  - id: the_ledger_of_faith
    displayName: The Ledger of Faith
    flavorText: Righteousness is credited to Abraham's account through faith alone,
      apart from works, establishing the pattern by which every believer is justified
      freely by God's grace.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Introduces a righteousness apart from the law, received by faith and
      credited ("counted"/"imputed") rather than earned by works, using Abraham's
      own justification - which occurred before his circumcision - as the scriptural
      proof, and contrasts the one trespass of Adam that brought condemnation to
      all with the one act of righteousness in Christ that brings justification and
      life.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_romans
    managerId: the_ledger_of_faith
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 503.6269964912326
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
    baseInkPerSecond: 25.18134982456163
    unlockAtVerseIndex: 81
    managerName: 
    managerFlavorText: 
    managerUnlockLevel: 0
    managerUnlockAtVerseIndex: 0
    managerBonusMultiplier: 0.25
    managerUnlockCost: 0
    submanagers: []
  - id: the_newness_of_life
    displayName: The Newness of Life
    flavorText: Buried with Christ through baptism into his death, believers rise
      to walk in newness of life, no longer slaves to sin but alive in the Spirit
      with no condemnation.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Answers the objection that grace should be exploited to keep sinning,
      by explaining the believer's union with Christ's death and resurrection through
      baptism, describes the ongoing internal struggle against indwelling sin even
      for one who delights in God's law, and closes with the assurance that life
      in the Spirit brings no condemnation and that nothing in creation can separate
      believers from the love of God in Christ Jesus.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_romans
    managerId: the_newness_of_life
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 3574.0736945012754
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
    baseInkPerSecond: 178.70368472506377
    unlockAtVerseIndex: 138
    managerName: 
    managerFlavorText: 
    managerUnlockLevel: 0
    managerUnlockAtVerseIndex: 0
    managerBonusMultiplier: 0.25
    managerUnlockCost: 0
    submanagers: []
  - id: the_wild_olive_branch
    displayName: The Wild Olive Branch
    flavorText: Israel's stumbling opens the door for the Gentiles to be grafted
      in like a wild olive branch onto the cultivated tree, with a promised future
      when all Israel shall be saved.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Explains that God's word has not failed even though most of Israel has
      not believed, because true Israel was never merely physical descent but God's
      own sovereign election (illustrated through Isaac/Ishmael and Jacob/Esau),
      describes Israel's present stumbling as the very means by which salvation has
      become available to the Gentiles (pictured as a wild olive branch grafted into
      the cultivated tree), and looks forward to a future restoration in which "all
      Israel shall be saved."
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_romans
    managerId: the_wild_olive_branch
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 25364.015159478
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
